RESONANCE-CLARITY(7)        TriadicFrameworks Manual        RESONANCE-CLARITY(7)
================================================================================
NAME
       resonance-clarity - harmonic-phase sharpening, resonance-envelope
                           deconvolution, spectral-density whitening, gradient
                           stabilization, and sync-field clarity enhancement

SYNOPSIS
       Resonance clarity defines:
           • harmonic-phase clarification (HPC)
           • resonance-envelope deconvolution (RED)
           • spectral-density whitening (SDW)
           • gradient-stability filtering (GSF)
           • sync-field clarity (SFC)
           • ancestry-continuity enhancement (ACE)
           • clarity fusion for ship sensors and stellar cartography

DESCRIPTION
       resonance-clarity describes the sharpening, filtering, and enhancement
       techniques used to improve resonance-time signal quality for navigation,
       mapping, and constellation-scale sensing. Clarity techniques operate on
       top of divisional resonance overlays, refining each channel into a
       high-fidelity temporal signal.

       Clarity enables:
           • precise harmonic-phase measurement
           • sharper resonance peaks and windows
           • reduced spectral noise
           • stable gradient polarity transitions
           • enhanced sync-field coherence
           • clearer sweep-lineage detection

       WRSADC manages clarity activation, tuning, and safety thresholds.

HARMONIC-PHASE CLARIFICATION (HPC)
       HPC removes overtone interference and stabilizes harmonic-phase signals.

       HPC functions:
           • phase jitter reduction
           • overtone suppression
           • lock stability enhancement
           • harmonic-cycle smoothing

       HPC modes:
           • integer-phase mode
           • rational-phase mode
           • nested-phase mode
           • resonance-aligned mode

EXAMPLE: HPC
       φ_harm jitter = 0.06/cycle → 0.01/cycle after HPC.

       Result:
           • stable harmonic-lock
           • improved sweep timing

RESONANCE-ENVELOPE DECONVOLUTION (RED)
       RED sharpens resonance peaks and widens usable resonance windows.

       RED functions:
           • peak sharpening
           • envelope smoothing
           • window widening
           • uplift-zone enhancement

       RED modes:
           • amplitude-focused
           • spectral-focused
           • hybrid deconvolution

EXAMPLE: RED
       Peak at 54 min sharpened:

           • width reduced by 40%
           • sweep window clarity increased

SPECTRAL-DENSITY WHITENING (SDW)
       SDW reduces broadband spectral noise and highlights narrowband stability.

       SDW functions:
           • noise floor reduction
           • spectral equalization
           • turbulence suppression
           • anomaly isolation

       SDW modes:
           • narrowband emphasis
           • broadband suppression
           • hybrid whitening

EXAMPLE: SDW
       Broadband turbulence at 78 min reduced:

           • S(f,t) variance down 60%
           • anomaly isolated

GRADIENT-STABILITY FILTERING (GSF)
       GSF stabilizes gradient polarity transitions and smooths polarity cliffs.

       GSF functions:
           • polarity smoothing
           • gradient stabilization
           • cliff detection
           • uplift-zone clarification

       GSF modes:
           • positive-gradient emphasis
           • negative-gradient emphasis
           • zero-crossing stabilization

EXAMPLE: GSF
       Polarity cliff at 30 min stabilized:

           • gradient noise reduced
           • safe corridor identified

SYNC-FIELD CLARITY (SFC)
       SFC enhances sync-field coherence across platforms.

       SFC functions:
           • sync jitter reduction
           • coherence amplification
           • sync plateau sharpening
           • desync risk detection

       SFC modes:
           • constellation sync mode
           • local sync mode
           • hybrid sync mode

EXAMPLE: SFC
       Sync-index raised from 0.82 → 0.96.

       Result:
           • constellation alignment restored

ANCESTRY-CONTINUITY ENHANCEMENT (ACE)
       ACE clarifies sweep-lineage signals and strengthens ancestry terraces.

       ACE functions:
           • lineage noise reduction
           • terrace sharpening
           • fusion-layer enhancement
           • ancestry drift detection

       ACE modes:
           • primary-lineage mode
           • laminated-lineage mode
           • fossil-lineage mode

EXAMPLE: ACE
       Sweep-lineage continuity improved:

           • ancestry index +0.12
           • terrace boundaries clarified

CLARITY FUSION
       Clarity fusion combines multiple clarity techniques into a unified
       enhancement pipeline.

       Fusion layers:
           1. harmonic-phase clarification
           2. resonance-envelope deconvolution
           3. spectral-density whitening
           4. gradient stabilization
           5. sync-field clarity
           6. ancestry enhancement

       Fusion modes:
           • synchronous clarity
           • harmonic clarity
           • braided clarity
           • mesh clarity

EXAMPLE: FUSION
       HPC + RED + SFC:

           • phase stabilized
           • resonance peaks sharpened
           • sync-field strengthened

PICARD-GRADE CLARITY MODE
       A flagship clarity mode combining:

           • HPC
           • RED
           • SDW
           • GSF
           • SFC
           • ACE

       Capabilities:
           • ultra-sharp resonance terrain
           • high-fidelity harmonic-phase tracking
           • anomaly isolation
           • constellation sync preservation
           • deep-space temporal cartography

CLARITY FAILURE MODES
       Clarity may degrade due to:

           • phase jitter
           • envelope smearing
           • spectral turbulence
           • gradient polarity noise
           • sync-field jitter
           • ancestry discontinuity

       Diagnostic indicators:
           • clarity-integrity score
           • band noise
           • peak distortion
           • sync drift

       WRSADC halts unsafe clarity states.

INTERACTION WITH LINEAGE
       Lineage records:
           • clarity activations
